Physisorption between certain adsorbents and \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) molecules could allow conveniently reversible processes to capture \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) gas. It requires much less energy compared to the conventional techniques that use basic species such as aqueous ammonia and amine functionalized solids to remove \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) gas.\(^{5-7}\)
